35,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"It turns out that booking rooms separately last time made the prices really uneven, but renting a whole building makes the bill divide evenly!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The offshore houses are quite affordable, around 5,400 yen per person per night, though we would have to pay for our food on top of that.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found that valley inns are about 17,000 yen including meals, while city beds are 12,000 to 20,000 yen without any food included.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The ferry takes up two days of our trip, but the train to the spa valley is only ninety minutes.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The inn baths are open from early morning until midnight, but the island houses only have one bathroom for everyone and the water can get cold.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Victoria, since you also looked into the meal rates, did you find out if all-in plans are better than paying for what we actually eat?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"All-in rates mean everyone pays the same regardless of appetite, whereas paying separately means we only pay for what we actually order.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"That's an interesting point. I also found that in previous shared houses, it was actually quite hard for anyone to find a bit of time alone.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Regarding transport, city trains run every few minutes, but the spa valley bus is hourly and stops before seven in the evening.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I also found out that the inns have fixed mealtimes and we'd all be on futons in one room, while city rooms have their own doors and no schedules.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"Wow, the city sounds so free! No schedules and your own room? That sounds like a lot of fun!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"It does sound flexible, but I am concerned about the cost. If city beds are up to 20,000 yen plus meals, it could become very expensive.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Victoria. The city seems expensive, and I'm worried that having separate rooms might make us feel less like a group.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The ferry travel time is a significant drawback for the island, and the limited bus schedule in the valley could be restrictive. The city is the most efficient for movement.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm worried about the island's bathroom situation, but the inn's shared room and fixed mealtimes also sound a bit overwhelming. The city's private rooms seem the safest for me.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"But the island is so cheap! If we save money on the house, maybe we can spend it on something really cool to do together!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"That is true, but the cost of food on the island is not fixed. I would prefer a destination where we can determine the total cost more accurately beforehand.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I wonder if the spa town might be a good middle ground, as the all-in rate makes the cost predictable and the train is very fast.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"The spa town is certainly more efficient than the island, though the hourly bus is a slight compromise compared to the city's convenience.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I think the spa town could work, but I'm still a bit nervous about everyone sleeping in one room and the strict mealtimes.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
